cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mewtwo in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mewtwo: a reproducible catalogue of side-channel and fault-injection attacks on the NIST post-quantum cryptography standards"
abstract: >-
  Mewtwo reproduces published physical attacks (side-channel and fault) against
  the NIST post-quantum cryptography standards (ML-KEM, ML-DSA, SLH-DSA, FN-DSA,
  HQC) and evaluates whether they still hold on modern deployed hardware and
  toolchains — primarily a Raspberry Pi 5 (Cortex-A76, AArch64). Negative and
  constant-time results are documented with the same rigour as successful breaks.
type: software
